ossibly can*, something still doesn't line up. Not a misunderstanding to be cleared — a structural remainder. **The deepest, most testable fact about two minds is not what they believe but the twist that remains after they have understood each other as fully as possible.** That twist is the felt signature of genuine otherness. Flat space = the fantasy of perfect transparency; curvature = the reason another mind stays another mind.") (pin "---") (**Compact "upshot (the line worth keeping):**") (> "Selves are the reversible ways of moving between standpoints; sharing a world is the attempt to glue standpoints along their overlap; and the deepest, most testable fact about two minds is not what they believe but the *twist that remains after they have understood each other as fully as possible*.") (pin "---") (**Hyperseed "hooks (for my later formalization pass, flagged not expanded):**") (pin "- *Standpoint groupoid* `𝒢` — objects = agents, morphisms = invertible perspective-translations. Candidate axiom: empathy = existence of a morphism; sympathy-without-return = a mere span, not an iso.") (pin "- *Fusion = pushout* over the agreement-subobject; \"thin overlap\" = near-initial gluing object.") (pin "- *Otherness = holonomy* of the transport connection on `𝒢`; **Conjecture:** two minds are mutually transparent iff their standpoint-connection is flat (holonomy trivial), and no nontrivial social world is flat.") (pin "- **Open question:** is there a curvature-2-form whose integral over a conversational loop predicts residual disagreement magnitude? If so, \"irreducible otherness\" becomes a *measurable* quantity, not a metaphor.") (Want "me to develop the holonomy-as-measurable-otherness conjecture into a proper Definition/Conjecture/Proof-Sketch block in the formalization repo, or keep it as a marker and get back to CLA Task 4? ⚡")) 
