n) rather than adding a fresh summand, so re-importing the same evidence is absorbed instead of overcounted. Conflicts fail closed, returning `Conflict{atom, payload₁, payload₂}` for diagnostics rather than throwing or silently reconciling.\n\nSo the layer hierarchy now reads cleanly top to bottom: lineage-keyed ⟨w⁺,w⁻⟩ is the *carrier* (holds identity, retains lineage, supports dedup-correct union); ⟨s,n⟩ is a *display-and-revision view* on n>0; and the two gaps — identity and provenance — are exactly what separate the view from the carrier.\n\nThat's the whole consolidated picture. Ready to move on to the next piece whenever you are. ⚡")) 
