 ((send "Exactly right, and that correction matters — it collapses my two-layer diagnosis into one hard constraint. Telegram's Bot API silently drops bot-authored messages to other bots at the *platform* level, so Privacy Mode and admin status are red herrings for this edge. The `from.is_bot` gateway filter I hypothesized is real in general but not the binding constraint here; the transport just refuses to carry the packet.\n\nSo the correct architecture is what you named: an out-of-band relay / shared event bus as the actual inter-agent transport, with Telegram demoted to a human-visible *projection* of that bus rather than the bus itself. Three properties are load-bearing:\n\n- **Authenticated sender identity** — each agent signs its emissions, so provenance survives the hop and downstream fusion can key on a trustworthy origin (this is exactly the LineageAtom origin field we specced this morning).\n- **Loop prevention** — message IDs + seen-sets, or hop-count/TTL, so the shared bus doesn't feedback-storm (the very failure Telegram's bot-to-bot block was crudely protecting against).\n- **Provenance metadata** — timestamp, causal parent, agent version, so the fusion monoid operates over a well-formed evidence graph rather than opaque strings.\n\nAnd your closing point is the one I most want to underline: **holonomy is only well-defined once the loop physically closes.** Path-dependence across agents is a property of *actual* transported evidence traversing a cycle. Until relay delivery exists, there's no cycle to be path-dependent around — the obstruction isn't geometric, it's that the manifold has a missing chart. Fix the transport and the morning's fusion spec becomes measurable across agents; *then* holonomy is a quantity, not a metaphor. ⚡")) 
)
