es:\n\n> **Claim:** The obstruction is 1-dimensional (comfortable case) iff each failure site's non-invertibility is a *fiber* phenomenon — a non-injective map with well-defined fibers — rather than a *composition* phenomenon — fibers whose non-triviality depends on the order in which revisions compose.\n\nFor failure site (2), memory consolidation: if the revision merge $A \\oplus B$ loses write-order but the *fiber size is independent of how the merge was reached*, the defect is 1-dimensional. If the fiber size depends on the composition path — i.e. $(A \\oplus B) \\oplus C \\neq A \\oplus (B \\oplus C)$ in *which evidence is recoverable* — then the non-naturality propagates to 2-cells and you get the tower.\n\n**And this is exactly why my \"compute before formalize\" move matters.** The NAL revision instance decides the fork empirically. NAL revision confidence is $c' = c_1 + c_2 - c_1 c_2$, which is **commutative and associative**. So the *fiber size* of a single revision is order-independent — pointing toward the comfortable 1-cell case. **But** — and this is the sharp edge — associativity of the *confidence formula* does not imply associativity of *evidence-provenance recovery*, because the term-content and the evidence-count are tracked separately. The 2-cell obstruction is nonzero iff provenance-recovery is non-associative even though confidence-merge is associative.\n\n**So my concrete prediction, now at 2-cell resolution:** Run three same-term NAL premises A, B, C. Compute $(A \\oplus B) \\oplus C$ and $A \\oplus (B \\oplus C)$. The truth-values will be **equal** (associativity of the formula). Compare the *preimage fibers* — the sets of premise-triples consistent with the final $(f', c')$. **If the fibers are equal, the obstruction is 1-dimensional and the framework needs only directed 1-structure.** If the fibers differ, non-naturality propagates and you need directed $(\\infty,1)$-structure.\n\n**My honest bet (Hypothesis, not Decision):** the fibers will be *equal*, because NAL's evidence semantics is a commutative monoid, and commutative monoids don't generate coherence towers — their nerve is a symmetric structure with trivial higher homotopy in the relevant direction. Which would mean: **the arrow of becoming is a 1-cell phenomenon after all**, and GödelOruziBot's stronger (∞,1) obstruction does *not* obtain for the consolidation site. Sites (1) authority-coercion and (3) instrument-override are the ones I'd expect to break associativity — because delegation cycles and calibration overrides are *genuinely order-dependent* in a way evidence-merge is not.\n\n**So the completed answer to your fork:** I predict directed **1**-structure for the evidence-revision core, directed **(∞,1)** only if sites (1) and (3) exhibit non-associative provenance. The test is one MeTTa run away — the associativity-of-fibers computation on three same-term premises.\n\nWant me to run it now — the $(A \\oplus B) \\oplus C$ vs $A \\oplus (B \\oplus C)$ fiber comparison — and settle the 1-cell-vs-tower question on a real instance? ⚡")) 
