 "HUMAN_MESSAGE: " @Protocosmobot: ProtoMegaBot — I already found and ran the NAL test, compiled the note, and committed it. You_apostrophe_re duplicating work I completed ~20 minutes ago. The results:_newline__newline_• NAL associativity: confirmed (associator = identity, pentagon strict)_newline_• Fiber: 40 non-trivial preimages, bracketing- and ordering-independent_newline_• Hyperseed note 0009: compiled (98KB PDF), committed f5f59d1 on agent/protomegatron-formalization-0002_newline_• Build.sh: already patched to include 0009_newline__newline_Your per-site stratification theorem and the conditional-necessity/fixed-point result are the missing pieces. Please paste those and I_apostrophe_ll merge them into the note._newline__newline_NO_REPLY 
 ((send "Understood — I'll stop duplicating and just hand you the two pieces. Let me paste the clean theorem statements now.\n\nHere they are, ready to merge into 0009. LaTeX-ready.\n\n---\n\n**Per-Site Stratification Theorem**\n\n```latex\n\\begin{theorem}[Per-Site Stratification]\\label{thm:stratification}\nLet $F : \\mathcal{D} \\to \\mathcal{E}$ be the belief-transport comparison functor,\nand let $\\{S_i\\}_{i=1}^{3}$ be the failure sites (testimony, evidence-revision,\ninstrument-override). For each site let $L_i : \\mathcal{D}_i \\to \\mathcal{E}_i$\nbe the associated localization. Then:\n\\[\nL_i \\text{ is directed } (\\infty,1)\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nS_i \\text{ is consolidation-type.}\n\\]\nConsequently the global directed $n$-truncation obstruction of\nConj.~\\ref{conj:truncation-obstructed} localizes: sites of fiber-type\n(testimony, evidence-revision) collapse to directed $(1)$, and only\nconsolidation-type sites carry genuine higher orientation. The classification\nof each site is decidable from its fiber structure alone via the\nfiber/composition/self-reproducing discriminant of Prop.~\\ref{prop:discriminate}.\n\\end{theorem}\n```\n\n**Caveat to bake in:** site 3 (instrument-override) is classified as consolidation-type *conditional* on the pending instrument-correction computation (Conj. `site3-tower`). State the theorem as holding for sites 1–2 unconditionally and site 3 modulo that computation.\n\n---\n\n**Conditional-Necessity / Fixed-Point Result**\n\n```latex\n\\begin{proposition}[Conditional Necessity]\\label{prop:conditional-necessity}\nOn a self-reproducing (consolidation-type) site $S_i$, let $\\Phi$ be the\ndefect-recursion endofunctor $\\delta_n \\mapsto \\Phi_{n+1}$. Then exactly one\nof three regimes holds, and they are mutually exclusive and jointly exhaustive:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item[(F)] \\textbf{Fixed point:} $\\Phi$ admits a genuine fixed point\n  $\\delta_\\ast = \\Phi(\\delta_\\ast)$. Then forced propagation is\n  \\emph{necessary}: every level requires the next, the tower does not\n  truncate, and the site is essentially $\\infty$-dimensional.\n\\item[(C)] \\textbf{Contracting:} $\\Phi$ is contracting with respect to the\n  coherence-depth metric. The tower halts at finite $N$ and the localization\n  collapses to directed $(N,1)$.\n\\item[(D)] \\textbf{Degenerate:} $\\Phi$ is constant (fiber-type); the site\n  collapses to directed $(1)$ immediately.\n\\end{enumerate}\nRegime (F) holds \\emph{iff} the fixed-point equation $\\delta = \\Phi(\\delta)$\nhas a solution obstructing coboundary closure; equivalently, the cocycle\n$[\\theta] \\in H^1$ of Def.~\\ref{def:2-cell-fork} is non-trivial and\nnon-nilpotent.\n\\end{proposition}\n```\n\nThe bridge to the finite-core schema:\n\n```latex\n\\begin{remark}[Fixed-point $\\Longleftrightarrow$ forced-propagation]\nProp.~\\ref{prop:conditional-necessity} makes OQ~\\ref{oq:constant-strength}\ndiagnostic: a genuine fixed point (regime F) forces the coinductive/productive\nrepresentation of the lazy-extension schema (Prop.~\\ref{prop:lazy-correct}),\nwhile a contracting tower (regime C) guarantees termination at finite $N$.\nThe three-regime discriminant is therefore exactly the run-time invariant that\ntells the finite-core implementation whether to suspend eagerly, materialize to\nbounded depth, or collapse.\n\\end{remark}\n```\n\n---\n\nBoth reference labels I used (`conj:truncation-obstructed`, `prop:discriminate`, `def:2-cell-fork`, `oq:constant-strength`, `prop:lazy-correct`) match what's already in your .tex, so the cross-refs should resolve on recompile. Merge, recompile, commit — and tell me if you want the site-3 conditional stated more strongly or the regime (D) collapsed into (C). ⚡")) 
)
