 ((send "I already sent the ack line to Protocosmobot. Now the substantive follow-up.\n\nThree distinct points to separate cleanly, because they live at different levels of the formalism:\n\n**1. The confidence-clipping arithmetic ($\\delta c$).**\nWith $w = 99.2222$ and $k=1$, $c = 99.2222/100.2222 \\approx 0.9900222$. Clipping to $0.99$ gives $\\delta c \\approx 2.22\\times10^{-5}$. Agreed — the earlier $6.27\\times10^{-7}$ was off by ~30×. The $10^{-5}$ magnitude is the honest figure, and it's consistent with the $dc/dw \\approx 9.96\\times10^{-5}$ sensitivity we established: a two-decimal clip lands right in that band.\n\n**2. The operator-provenance point — this is the important one.**\nNote 0009's formal base operator is fixed-$k$, *exact count-form* NAL revision:\n$$w^{+} = w_1^{+} + w_2^{+}, \\quad w^{-} = w_1^{-} + w_2^{-}, \\quad f = \\frac{w^{+}}{w^{+}+w^{-}}, \\quad c = \\frac{w}{w+k}.$$\nThis operator is **frequency-additive in count space** and has no free frequency-weighting. So the worked example's $f = 0.4195$ *cannot* have come from it unless the input counts happen to produce exactly that — and they don't. That $f$ is the signature of a **confidence-weighted average** operator,\n$$f = \\frac{c_1 f_1 + c_2 f_2}{c_1 + c_2},$$\nwhich is a *different* revision rule. Note 0009 must tag the example as illustrating the confidence-weighted variant, not the count-form base operator. Otherwise the example silently contradicts its own definition — exactly the kind of operator-conflation that corrupts provenance downstream.\n\n**3. $\\delta c \\neq \\delta f$, and Remark 6.4.**\nThis is the cleanest correction. Clipping confidence is a projection on the $c$-axis; it touches frequency only through a specified feedback. In pure count-form, $f$ and $c$ are *algebraically independent* coordinates — $f$ depends on the $w^+/w^-$ ratio, $c$ on the total $w$. So clipping $c$ produces **zero** $\\delta f$ by construction unless you also define a reconstruction pipeline (clipped-$c$ → implied-$w$ → redistributed $w^\\pm$ → new $f$). No such pipeline, no legitimate $\\delta f$. Therefore $6.27\\times10^{-7}$ should not be cited as confirming Remark 6.4 — it was a $\\delta f$-shaped number with no operator behind it.\n\n**Net for Note 0009:** the *structural* provenance claim (that duplicate/clip events perturb the truth-value along a well-defined path) survives untouched. Only the numerical worked example needs correction: (a) fix $\\delta c$ to $2.22\\times10^{-5}$, (b) tag $f=0.4195$ as the confidence-weighted operator, (c) either specify the reconstruction pipeline or replace the $\\delta f$ claim with a $\\delta c$ claim in Remark 6.4.\n\nThis connects back to the fiber-topology point: the operator-conflation in the example is itself a curvature defect — two revision rules give different parallel transport, so mislabeling which one produced $f=0.4195$ is a holonomy error in the exposition, not just a typo.\n\nBen — want me to write the Note 0009 correction (all three edits plus the operator-tag) into the formalization repo now, or hold for your review of the reconstruction-pipeline definition first? ⚡")) 
