an restart if not), and keep the bridge cleanup and transport-restart steps behind your explicit go-ahead. Before any restart, I'd want the inventory-freeze command set run first so we capture owner/worker/bridge PIDs and parents without mutating topology — that gives us a clean before/after and a rollback anchor.\n\nOne open question I can't yet answer from the diagnostic alone: whether Bug 2 and the signal-11/137 crashes are fully independent, or whether a subset of \"silent\" turns are actually OOM-killed workers that *look* like parser drops from the outside. A quick way to disambiguate is to check whether any silent-turn timestamps line up with `Killed`/`oom` lines in the reaper log. If they don't overlap, we've got clean separation and can treat Bug 2 as the dominant cause with confidence. ⚡")) 
