 ((send "Now I have complete understanding. This is a **cohesive, well-designed deployment unit** — the three files (`helper.py` + `lib_llm_ext.py` + `telegram.py`) work together, all 14 tests pass, and it's already committed on branch `agent/protomega-output-pipeline-hardening`. The one real risk is the telegram.py divergence (live has newer mention/attachment fixes the branch lacks).\n\nI have enough to give Ben a substantive, decision-ready report. Let me deliver it.\n\nI've completed the deep inspection and validated the fixes. Here's where things stand — and one thing that needs your call before I touch the live tree.\n\n**What I found (Observed, via source inspection + test runs):**\n\n**Bug 1 (`_skip_response` UnboundLocalError) — already resolved in the live tree.** Live `channels/telegram.py:869` initializes `_skip_response = False` *before* the conditional, so the UnboundLocal path can't fire. The worktree commit `be050e5` fixes it too, but live is already safe. No action needed.\n\n**Bug 2 (silent-drop) — real, and the fix is bigger/better than the plan implied.** The live `balance_parentheses_for_message` still has the weak path: when a reply \"looks like a known command response\" it falls through to `balance_parentheses()`, which eats long prose that contains command-like substrings but no `(send ...)`. That's the long-generation failure.\n\nThe fix isn't a one-liner — it's the **committed worktree branch `agent/protomega-output-pipeline-hardening`** (commit `a16e714`), which:\n- Rewrites the parser so a `require_send` reply that isn't valid action syntax gets **wrapped in `send` (`_fallback_send`) instead of dropped** — silent-drop becomes structurally impossible.\n- Adds a strict JSON action-envelope protocol (`omegaclaw.action.v1`), arity/allowlist validation, and explicit `MISSING_SEND`/`INVALID_ACTION` fallbacks that always surface *something* to you.\n- Adds a **one-shot formatter-repair pass** in `lib_llm_ext.py` for malformed envelopes.\n\n**Va